<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="hero">
  <h1>About Book Finder</h1>
  <p>A small server-side web application that turns raw book data into readable pages with statistics.</p>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>The API</h2>
  <p>Data comes from <a href="https://openlibrary.org/developers/api" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Library</a>,
    a free public API that needs no API key. The server calls it with Axios and shows the result with EJS.</p>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li><code>GET /search.json</code> searches books by anything, title, author or subject.</li>
    <li><code>GET /works/{id}.json</code> gives the details of one book.</li>
    <li><code>GET /works/{id}/ratings.json</code> gives the rating of a book.</li>
    <li><code>GET /authors/{id}.json</code> and <code>/authors/{id}/works.json</code> give an author and the author's books.</li>
    <li><code>GET /subjects/{subject}.json</code> gives the books of one subject.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>What the app adds</h2>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li>Checks the input on the server and explains problems in plain words.</li>
    <li>Counts books per decade, finds the most frequent authors and the book with the most editions.</li>
    <li>Cleans descriptions, builds rating bars and shows placeholders for missing covers.</li>
    <li>Pagination for search results, authors and subjects.</li>
    <li>Handles timeouts, rate limits and API errors without crashing.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

